course: dictionary
lesson: 10492
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. «The turntable spins so the food heats more evenly.» Here a turntable is the flat round plate inside a microwave. The words around it, such as food and heats, show you which meaning fits.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. Ask yourself: does my meaning make sense here? If you swap in "record player" for "turntable" in the microwave sentence, it stops making sense, so you have picked the wrong meaning.
explain: Some meanings are everyday, and some belong to a special subject. A DJ uses turntables to play music, and a history lesson about railways might talk about a big turntable that turns engines. Knowing the subject helps you choose the right meaning quickly.
fact: A turntable is the round flat part of a record player that spins the record.
fact: A turntable can also be any flat round platform that turns, such as one that turns trains around.
fact: «Turntable» is a noun, so you can have one turntable or many turntables.
fact: In a microwave oven, the turntable spins so the food heats more evenly.
fact: «Microwaves heat only the outer few centimetres of the food, and the heat then spreads inwards.»
exercise: «The turntable spins so the food heats more evenly.» Where would you find this turntable? | On a bookshelf | In a school hall | At the top of a hill | *Inside a microwave oven
exercise: DJ Mia sets up two turntables for the party. What is a turntable in this sentence? | A chair with wheels | *A deck that spins records so music can play | A large table for eating | A tall tower of speakers
exercise: In a history lesson, a big turntable is used for what? | To play music at a party | *To turn railway engines round to face the other way | To hold books on a shelf | To make bread rise
test: Ravi says a turntable must always be a music machine. Is he right? | No, a turntable is a kind of bread | Yes, turntables only play music | Yes, but only in a microwave | *No, a turntable can be any flat round platform that turns, such as one in a microwave
test: In the phrase «a microwave turntable», what does the word microwave tell you? | It means the turntable is very hot | It means the turntable plays music | It means the turntable is very small | *It tells you which kind of turntable: the one inside a microwave oven
exam: A word can have more than one meaning, so what should you check in the sentence? | Whether the word is long | Only the first meaning you ever learned | How many letters the word has | *Whether your chosen meaning makes sense in the sentence
